<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41453" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rĕ-suscĭto</span></b> ,
			āre, v. a., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to raise up again</i>, <i>rebuild</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">templum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lact. 4, 18, 5</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>To rouse again</i>, <i>revive</i>,
				<i>resuscitate</i>, freq. in the Christian
			writers, of the resurrection of the dead,
				<i><span class="en">Hier. in Psa. 33, 5</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">id. Ep. 103</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Tert. Res. Carn. 38</span></i>; Prud.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στεφ.</span> 6, 136; <i><span class="en">Vulg. Act. 2,
				32</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Johan. 6,
			39</span></i>.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b> (very rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">positam iram,</span>”
				<i>to revive</i>, <i>resuscitate</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					8, 474</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">veterem iram,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 14, 495</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">legatum,</span>”
				<i>to renew</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Dig. 34, 4, 27, § 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gratiam Dei,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg. 2
					Tim. 1, 6</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
